  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Op 0 (lo, hi): sets script_src_ptr."},
    {"at":11,"placement":"line","text":"Op 1 (lo, hi): sets script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":22,"placement":"line","text":"Op 2 (n, n bytes): copies the n bytes that follow in the script to script_dest_ptr and adds n to script_dest_ptr. script_src_ptr is then the end of the bytes. With bit 7: n and the bytes come from script_arg_stack."},
    {"at":30,"placement":"side","text":"Source = the bytes in the script."},
    {"at":41,"placement":"side","text":"Skip the bytes in the script."},
    {"at":50,"placement":"line","text":"Copies Y bytes from script_src_ptr to script_dest_ptr, last byte first."},
    {"at":58,"placement":"line","text":"Adds the count on the stack (0 = 256) to script_src_ptr and script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":67,"placement":"line","text":"Op 2 with bit 7: pops n bytes to script_dest_ptr, first pop first, and adds n to script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":93,"placement":"line","text":"Op 37 (n): copies n bytes from script_src_ptr to script_dest_ptr with all RAM (no ROM, no I/O) and adds n to both pointers."},
    {"at":108,"placement":"line","text":"Op 3 (n): copies n bytes from script_src_ptr to script_dest_ptr and adds n to both pointers."},
    {"at":112,"placement":"line","text":"Copies Y bytes (A = Y = count, 0 = 256) from script_src_ptr to script_dest_ptr and adds the count to both pointers."},
    {"at":116,"placement":"line","text":"Op 4 (n): swaps n bytes between script_src_ptr and script_dest_ptr with all RAM (no ROM, no I/O) and adds n to both pointers."},
    {"at":144,"placement":"line","text":"Op 5 (count, lo, hi): loop. The first time, it pushes an entry on script_loop_stack and jumps to the address. Each next time, it decrements the count and jumps again until the count is 0. Then it pops the entry and continues after the operands. Thus the code between the address and the op runs count + 1 times. With bit 7: the count comes from script_arg_stack. With a full loop stack, it continues after the operands."},
    {"at":148,"placement":"side","text":"Is this op 5 the top entry of the loop stack?"},
    {"at":187,"placement":"line","text":"Skips the operands: 3 bytes, or 2 bytes with bit 7."},
    {"at":205,"placement":"line","text":"Pushes address lo, address hi, count, script_ptr lo and hi, then jumps to the address."},
    {"at":254,"placement":"line","text":"Pulls the new script_ptr (hi, then lo) from the CPU stack."},
    {"at":261,"placement":"line","text":"Op 6: SEI (disables the interrupts)."},
    {"at":263,"placement":"line","text":"Op 7: CLI (enables the interrupts)."},
    {"at":265,"placement":"line","text":"Op 8 (lo, hi): calls the script at the address. It pushes script_ptr on script_return_stack; opcode $ff of the called script returns."},
    {"at":292,"placement":"line","text":"Op 9 (lo, hi): jumps to the machine code at the address. The RTS of that code returns to the interpreter loop."},
    {"at":305,"placement":"line","text":"Op 10 (n): adds n (0 = 256) to script_src_ptr."},
    {"at":313,"placement":"line","text":"Op 11 (n): adds n (0 = 256) to script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":321,"placement":"line","text":"Op 12 (n): writes script_fill_byte to n bytes at script_dest_ptr and adds n to script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":339,"placement":"line","text":"Op 13 (byte): sets script_fill_byte."},
    {"at":345,"placement":"line","text":"Op 14 (n, n bytes): pushes the n bytes that follow in the script on script_arg_stack. The first byte is on top, so the next pops give the bytes in script order. The operands always come from the script."},
    {"at":370,"placement":"line","text":"Op 15 (n): adds n to script_arg_index. The n bytes above the top become stack bytes again. The operand always comes from the script."},
    {"at":379,"placement":"line","text":"Op 16: empties script_arg_stack."},
    {"at":384,"placement":"line","text":"Op 17 (n): removes n bytes from script_arg_stack. The operand always comes from the script."},
    {"at":397,"placement":"line","text":"Op 18: does nothing."},
    {"at":398,"placement":"line","text":"Op 19 (a, b, c): writes a to current_colour and script_op19_byte1, b to script_op19_byte2, c to script_op19_byte3."},
    {"at":416,"placement":"line","text":"Op 20: calls $0915 (X = shape_x0, Y = shape_y0) and $0918 of the jump table at $0900, then adds script_step_x to shape_x0 and script_step_y to shape_y0."},
    {"at":423,"placement":"line","text":"Calls $0918, then adds the steps to shape_x0 and shape_y0."},
    {"at":441,"placement":"line","text":"Op 21 (x): sets shape_x0."},
    {"at":447,"placement":"line","text":"Op 22 (y): sets shape_y0."},
    {"at":453,"placement":"line","text":"Op 23 (dx): sets script_step_x."},
    {"at":459,"placement":"line","text":"Op 24 (dy): sets script_step_y."},
    {"at":465,"placement":"line","text":"Op 25 (x, y): sets shape_x1 and shape_y1, then jumps to $091b. In this build $091b is cold_start."},
    {"at":465,"placement":"side","text":"JMP $091b: in this build $091b is cold_start, the first byte after the 9 entries of entry_jump_table. No script uses op 25."},
    {"at":478,"placement":"line","text":"Op 26 (a): calls $0918 with A = a, X = shape_x0, Y = shape_y0, then adds script_step_x to shape_x0 and script_step_y to shape_y0."},
    {"at":488,"placement":"line","text":"Op 27: pushes script_src_ptr on script_arg_stack (lo on top), for a later op with bit 7."},
    {"at":502,"placement":"line","text":"Op 28: pushes script_dest_ptr on script_arg_stack (lo on top), for a later op with bit 7."},
    {"at":517,"placement":"line","text":"Op 29: pushes shape_x0 on script_arg_stack."},
    {"at":525,"placement":"line","text":"Op 30: pushes shape_y0 on script_arg_stack."},
    {"at":533,"placement":"line","text":"Op 31: reads the byte at script_src_ptr into pixel_value and adds 1 to script_src_ptr."},
    {"at":544,"placement":"line","text":"Op 32 (n): adds n to shape_y0."},
    {"at":553,"placement":"line","text":"Op 33, and a subroutine: SEI, then $01 bits 0-1 = 0 (all RAM: no BASIC, no KERNAL, no I/O)."},
    {"at":561,"placement":"line","text":"Op 34, and a subroutine: $01 bits 0-1 = 1 (BASIC, KERNAL and I/O on), then CLI."},
    {"at":569,"placement":"line","text":"Op 35 (lo, hi): jumps to the script at the address when script_condition is not 0."},
    {"at":591,"placement":"line","text":"Op 36 (n): subtracts n from script_dest_ptr."},
    {"at":608,"placement":"line","text":"Adds 2 to script_arg_index. Output X = the new script_arg_index."},
    {"at":610,"placement":"line","text":"Adds 1 to script_arg_index. Output X = the new script_arg_index."},
    {"at":615,"placement":"line","text":"Adds A to script_src_ptr. A = 0 adds 256."},
    {"at":627,"placement":"line","text":"Adds A to script_dest_ptr. A = 0 adds 256."}
